The document’s skeleton — containers, regions, sections, the website page-set, and the section break.

<section #ag-article | `<article>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article>`.

<code-block #code:ag-article-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.

<section | Conclusion>
The paper concludes here.
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-article-1>
<meta type=article>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
  <date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>

<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.

<section | Conclusion>
The paper concludes here.
</minipage>

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=article&gt; at the top with no
&lt;article&gt; wrapper. The structural plugin generates the &lt;article&gt;
container and the three region wrappers. &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; is
promoted to &lt;article-title&gt;; &lt;meta&gt; itself survives inside
&lt;article-front&gt;.*

<section #ag-article-back | `<article-back>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article-back>`.

<section #ag-article-body | `<article-body>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article-body>`.

<section #ag-article-front | `<article-front>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<article-front>`.

<section #ag-book | `<book>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<book>`.

<code-block #code:ag-book-1>
<meta type=book>
  <title | A Natural History of Elephants>
  <author | Jane Goodall>
</meta>

<chapter | Origins>
<section | Early ancestors>
Content here.

<chapter | Modern populations>
<section | African elephants>
Content here.
</code-block>

*(Rendered preview omitted — a book (`<meta type=book>` / `<chapter>`) is a whole-document structure, which a sealed preview box cannot host.)*

*Typical authoring path: &lt;meta type=book&gt; at the top with no &lt;book&gt;
wrapper. The structural plugin generates &lt;book&gt; + the three region
wrappers. Each book-part contains its own &lt;meta&gt; with the promoted
&lt;book-part-title&gt;; no &lt;book-part-meta&gt; wrapper.*

<section #ag-book-back | `<book-back>`>

